## Findings

All six are late findings. The suggested call for each is tech-debt, because each names test tooling, not a product file, and none changes an output that a user sees.

ADV-25 [Late finding; suggested call tech-debt; the orchestrator may take the careful one-fix-round call]
  src/__tests__/blog-posts-loader.adversarial.test.ts:77 builds a temp directory under the literal path /home/daniebo/.cache/opencode.
  That path exists on this machine only. mkdirSync with recursive true runs outside the try block.
  A user that cannot create /home/daniebo gets EACCES, and the case "surfaces a symlink to a directory named .md (ADV-22)" fails.
  CI runs "pnpm turbo run build lint check-types test --filter=www-reading-advantage..." on ubuntu-latest (.github/workflows/ci.yml).
  The www test script is "vitest run" (apps/www-reading-advantage/package.json), and vitest.config.ts includes src/**/*.test.ts.
  I did not run CI. P14 is a proxy only.
  The sibling tests use mkdtempSync in the OS temp directory (blog-posts-loader-symlink.test.ts:32, blog-posts-loader-dotfile.test.ts:31).
  The case passes on this machine only. The www CI job would fail at the later www push.
  A fix is a test-file edit. Under the role contract, a fix commit invalidates this result and the adversarial gate runs again.

ADV-26 [Late finding; suggested call tech-debt]
  The 2027 school year that master added to the home suite line has weak guards.
  P1: a changed year fails by name in en and zh, through the year class of the claims scanner.
  P11: a th year change from 2570 to 2571 passes all 1413 tests. A Thai year never matches the year class /20\d\d/.
  P9: removing the clause in en, th, and zh passes all 1413 tests. No test asserts that the year is present.
  P11: a Thai "STEM Advantage อยู่ในแผนงาน" passes. The new rule (www-batch-20261116.locale.test.ts:188-193) checks "on our roadmap" and "暂无日期" in every locale and checks no Thai phrase.
  Master guarded this line with an exact pin: expect(home).toBe(expected.home) in page.content.test.tsx at 968bde612. D5 removed that pin on the pilot side.
  The pilot asserts "2027" and "2570" on the badges, the roadmap note, and the six detail lines (www-batch-20261116.locale.test.ts:147-152, 228-233, 289-294).
  It does not assert them on pages.home.suite.description.

ADV-27 [Late finding; suggested call tech-debt]
  Expected copy data pins nothing, and the merge edited it.
  P11: noise in LABEL_COPY.*.home, in the en and th fields of ROW_B row 7, and in OVERVIEW_LABEL_COPY.en.description leaves all 1413 tests green.
  Static search: no test reads the en, th, or zh field of any ROW_A or ROW_B row. Lines 139-178 of www-batch-20261116.locale.test.ts read only key and old.
  LABEL_COPY has one reader: ".en.navigation" at page.content.test.tsx:300.
  EXPECTED_META, EXPECTED_AUX_COPY, OVERVIEW_LABEL_COPY, PAGE_COPY, and IMAGE_ALT have no importer outside the fixture.
  Master changed three LABEL_COPY.home strings and the ROW_B home strings in 968bde612, so the strings look pinned and are not.
  P4: the school-year control (page.content.test.tsx:439) uses APPROVED_SCHOOL_YEAR.en as its own sample, so it passes for any value of the constant.
  P11: APPROVED_SCHOOL_YEAR.th changes nothing in the suite, because the clearing of a Thai year clears no claim.

ADV-28 [Late finding; suggested call tech-debt]
  The Thai month class has controls for 4 of 12 months: ธันวาคม, มกราคม, พฤษภาคม, and พฤศจิกายน (through APPROVED_DATES.th).
  P5: deleting ธันวาคม fails by name. P11: deleting the other eight months passes all 1413 tests.
  A misspelled month name stays invisible. The pilot commit 733319505 added the class.
  The English class has a control for every month (page.content.test.tsx:188-202).

ADV-29 [Late finding; note; parity with the baseline]
  P8: a YAML syntax error in one post fails blog-posts-validation.test.ts at collection and names no post. The other 16 rules do not run.
  The baseline 635a604c8 parsed every post at module scope with no catch, so the behavior is the same.
  The rule failures of P7 name the post. The report claim "named in the failure" holds for rule violations, as proof-blog-merge.log shows.

ADV-30 [Late finding; note; static; not reproduced]
  blog-posts-loader.adversarial.test.ts:39 and :56-58 write a .mdx probe and an uppercase .MD probe into the real en posts directory.
  blog-blocks.test.ts:210 sweeps that directory. blog-draft.test.ts publishedEnglishCount reads every entry of it. blog-posts-validation.test.ts lists it.
  Under parallel files, an overlap would fail one reader. The strategy gate uses --maxWorkers=1. The CI test script does not.
  P12: ten parallel runs of the seven files all passed. The overlap window is a few milliseconds.

